Added a writePointsValidationEnabled boolean field to the Engine struct with a corresponding WithWritePointsValidationEnabled option function to control validation behavior. Wrapped all validation logic in the WritePoints method with a conditional check that defaults to enabled for backward compatibility. Added a BenchmarkValidToken test to measure validation performance and ensured dashboard axes are sorted consistently by name during export in convertCellView.

Refactor the MDAPI metric set activation logic to activate metric sets only once during initialization and deactivate them during MDAPI shutdown, rather than activating and deactivating them each time a performance counter queue is created. This change improves efficiency by reducing redundant activation and deactivation cycles that occur whenever createMDAPICommandQueue is called. Currently the code activates the metric set, creates the queue, then immediately deactivates it, which is unnecessary overhead. Plan: 1. Add an m_Activated member variable to the MDHelper class in MetricsDiscoveryHelper.h to track activation state. 2. Update MetricsDiscoveryHelper.cpp to initialize m_Activated in the constructor, check it in ActivateMetricSet and DeactivateMetricSet methods, and call DeactivateMetricSet in the destructor. 3. Remove the DeactivateMetricSet call from createMDAPICommandQueue in intercept_mdapi.cpp since deactivation will happen at shutdown.

