Removed the entire dist directory containing all compiled distribution files. This includes the commonjs bundle, esm module, browser build, minified javascript, and both css files. These build artifacts are now excluded from version control since they should be generated during the build process rather than committed.

# Improve ECharts Editor Layout and Fix Build Issues

The ECharts visual editor example currently stacks all components vertically, making it difficult to view the chart preview while editing configuration. This layout needs to be reorganized into a two-column grid for better usability. Additionally, there are build configuration issues in the FIS setup causing gh-pages deployment errors, CSS variable inconsistencies in the CXD theme, and a potential React warning in the Custom renderer when handling empty HTML content.

Plan: 1. Restructure examples/components/ECharts.tsx to use a grid layout with chart and editor on the left, form controls on the right. 2. Update fis-conf.js to fix SCSS file processing rules for different build environments. 3. Move body-bg and text-color from SASS variables to CSS custom properties in scss/themes/_cxd-variables.scss. 4. Fix src/renderers/Custom.tsx to use empty string instead of null for dangerouslySetInnerHTML.

