The gh-pages build is throwing errors and I suspect it's related to how SCSS files are being processed. Looking at fis-conf.js, there's a global fis.match rule for '_*.scss' files that applies parser transformations everywhere, but this conflicts with the publish environment. I should remove that global rule and only apply it within fis.media('dev'), then set release to false for the publish environment. While I'm at it, the CXD theme has body-bg and text-color defined as SASS variables but they should be CSS custom properties in the :root block for consistency with other theme variables. Also noticed the Custom renderer passes null to dangerouslySetInnerHTML when html is falsy, which could trigger React warnings - changing that to an empty string is safer.

