Hey, I need to add a size prop to our Button component so users can control whether buttons render as small, medium, or large. Right now the button only supports variant, icon, loading, and disabled props, but there's no way to adjust the actual size of the button itself. This is a common requirement when you need denser buttons in compact layouts or larger buttons for primary actions that need more visual weight.

The change should follow the same pattern we use for other props - add it to the interface definition, pass it through to the underlying Material-UI button component, and set a sensible default. I'll also need to update the documentation examples so users can see how to use the different sizes, add a story for visual testing, and write tests to verify each size renders with the correct CSS classes from Material-UI.

