Enable dynamic management of the mutable cache size by implementing methods to query the current storage usage and adjust the maximum allowed limit at runtime. Users need visibility into how much data is stored and the ability to shrink the cache to free up disk space without restarting the application. When the maximum size is reduced, the system must evict excess data in chunks to allow for periodic database compaction and avoid long blocking operations. Plan: 1. Update the cache implementation header to declare new size management APIs and helper structures for chunked eviction. 2. Refactor the core cache logic to support dynamic size limits and implement the eviction chunking mechanism. 3. Adjust existing tests to use the new public API and add a new test case to verify eviction behavior when reducing the cache size limit.

