# Display Latest Block Information in Dashboard

The dashboard needs to show the latest Polkadot block information to users. Currently, there's no visibility into blockchain state beyond account data. However, fetching block data on a continuous interval causes MetaMask to become unresponsive, similar to issues observed with account balance polling. The solution is to fetch the latest block once on component mount and display the block hash and number in a clean, readable format.

Plan: 1. Create a new LatestBlock component with proper state management, 2. Add a service function to fetch block data through the MetaMask snap, 3. Integrate the component into the Dashboard, 4. Modify the getBlock RPC handler to return structured block info instead of raw SignedBlock data, 5. Update tests to validate the new return type, 6. Ensure the fetch happens only once to avoid performance issues.

