Update the TypeScript type definitions to accurately reflect the mxGraph library's actual API behavior. Several properties and constructor parameters in the text shape class are currently marked as required when they should be optional, since the underlying implementation provides default values for them. This mismatch causes unnecessary friction for developers using the library, forcing them to specify values that mxGraph will use anyway.

Additionally, there are missing shape constants in the type definitions that exist in the actual mxGraph implementation. These constants are used throughout the codebase for identifying different shape types, and their absence from the type definitions means developers cannot get proper type checking and autocomplete support when working with rounded rectangle shapes.

The goal is to align the type definitions with the runtime behavior by marking appropriate properties and parameters as optional where defaults exist, and ensuring all shape constants are properly declared in the type system.

