# Add Default Label Layout Configuration for Line, Area, Column, and Bar Charts

## Background

Currently, when users enable labels on line, area, column, and bar charts without specifying a layout configuration, the labels may overlap or appear in suboptimal positions. This creates a poor user experience where chart labels are difficult to read or get cut off at plot boundaries.

## Problem

Users have to manually configure label layout strategies for basic chart types, even though there are sensible defaults that would work well for most use cases. The existing implementation passes label configurations directly through `transformLabel` without adding any automatic layout adjustments.

## Solution

Implement automatic default label layout configurations for line, area, column, and bar chart types. When a user enables labels but doesn't specify a layout, the system should automatically apply appropriate layout strategies:

- For line and area charts: limit labels to plot boundaries, adjust positions along paths and points, and hide labels that exceed bounds
- For column and bar charts: adjust interval positions, hide overlapping labels, adjust colors for visibility, and hide labels outside plot bounds

The implementation should respect user configurations - if a user explicitly sets a layout, that takes precedence over defaults.

## Plan

1. Modify the label handling functions in the adaptor files for each chart type
2. Add default layout arrays that get applied when labels are enabled but no layout is specified
3. Ensure user-provided layouts override the defaults
4. Add comprehensive test cases to verify default layouts are applied correctly
5. Test edge cases where labels are disabled or custom layouts are provided

