The current implementation relies on the route object passed into the export default function, but that value is captured at initialization and doesn't update during client-side navigation. I need to remove the route dependency from the plugin arguments and instead check the browser's location directly within the subscription callback. Specifically, inside the PRODUCT_VIEW event handler, I will swap the route.path check for a window.location.href check to ensure we are actually on the product page when firing the viewedProduct function. Since this logic runs in the browser, I must also add a guard to ensure window is defined before accessing location properties. Once the logic is corrected, I will bump the package version to mark the release.

