The ignore logic is scattered and only handles symbols right now through the ignoreChange function. I should consolidate all ignore checks into one place and make it more comprehensive. Renaming ignoreChange to ignoreProperty makes the purpose clearer. I can add a check for options.ignoreUnderscores to skip any property starting with an underscore, and bring the ignoreKeys check into this function as well. Then I need to update all the handler methods that call ignoreChange to use the new ignoreProperty function instead. The type definitions need to document both ignoreKeys and ignoreUnderscores options, the readme should explain how to use them, and tests should verify that property assignment, definition, and deletion all respect these new ignore rules.

