Hey, I need to clean up some technical debt across the codebase. There's a bunch of maintenance work to tackle. First, the Visible component in packages/atomic-layout/src/components/Visible.tsx has gotten pretty messy with all the manual media query building logic. I want to simplify it by leveraging the useResponsiveQuery hook that already exists, which should make the component way more readable.

Then there's the memoizeWith utility in packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/memoizeWith/memoizeWith.ts and its test file packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/memoizeWith/memoizeWith.spec.ts. The typing could be tighter with proper generics, and the test is using a manual callsCount variable which feels hacky. I should switch to jest.fn() for cleaner mocking.

Finally, I noticed we have some utility functions that nobody's actually using anymore. The spread function in packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/spread/index.ts, packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/spread/spread.spec.ts, and packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/spread/spread.ts can go. Same with the when function in packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/when/index.ts, packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/when/when.spec.ts, and packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/when/when.ts. Let's remove that dead code to keep the repo lean.

--- packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/memoizeWith/memoizeWith.spec.ts ---
import memoizeWith from './memoizeWith'

describe('memoizeWith', () => {
  describe('given memoized a function', () => {
    let callsCount = 0
    const memoizeWithIdentity = memoizeWith((n) => n)
    const factorial = memoizeWithIdentity((num) => {
      callsCount += 1
      return Array<number>(num)
        .fill(0)
        .map((_, i) => i + 1)
        .reduce<number>((acc, n) => acc * n, 1)
    })

    afterEach(() => {
      callsCount = 0
    })

    it('should return the result when called', () => {
      expect(factorial(5)).toEqual(120)
    })

    it('should return memoized result when given the same arguments', () => {
      factorial(5)
      factorial(5)
      factorial(5)
      expect(callsCount).toEqual(0)
    })

    it('should execute anew for each unique set of arguments', () => {
      factorial(3)
      factorial(4)
      expect(callsCount).toEqual(2)
    })
  })
})

--- packages/atomic-layout-core/src/utils/functions/memoizeWith/memoizeWith.ts ---
interface Cache {
  [key: string]: any
}

export default function memoizeWith(saltGenerator: (...args: any[]) => string) {
  const cache: Cache = {}

  return (func: (...args: any[]) => any) =>
    function(...args: any[]) {
      const key = saltGenerator(...args)

      if (!(key in cache)) {
        cache[key] = func(...args)
      }

      return cache[key]
    }
}

