[Azure/aks-engine: AKS Engine: Units of Kubernetes on Azure!]

Hey, I need to update the Linux VHD image versions we're using for our AKS clusters. The team just released new VHD builds from early September that include some important updates - specifically the generate aggregated API certs script is now pre-installed, which will help reduce our cloud-init payload overhead during cluster provisioning. I need to bump the image version references in our Azure environment configuration and make sure we have the corresponding release notes files in place for both Ubuntu 16.04 and 18.04 variants.

Plan: 1. Update the image version strings in our Azure environment configuration for both Ubuntu variants. 2. Add the new release notes documentation files that correspond to these VHD versions. 3. Double-check that all version numbers are consistent across the codebase.

