[guardian/prosemirror-typerighter: A Prosemirror plugin to manage document validation.]

Users need the ability to toggle the Typerighter validation UI on and off to work without distractions. This requires implementing a toggle mechanism in the sidebar that controls whether the plugin interface and decorations are visible. The solution involves creating a new Sidebar component that manages active/inactive state, adding close and open controls, and wiring the toggle state to the plugin configuration so decorations are hidden when inactive. Changes are needed in src/css/Sidebar.scss and src/css/index.scss for styling the closed state, src/ts/components/Controls.tsx and src/ts/components/Results.tsx for UI updates, src/ts/components/Sidebar.tsx and src/ts/components/icons/CloseIcon.tsx as new components, and src/ts/createTyperighterPlugin.ts and src/ts/createView.tsx to integrate the state management.

