Simplified the del() method across six Spring Data versions by replacing the complex executeAsync() implementation with a direct write() call, enabling proper pipeline participation. Removed the unused checkExecution() and executeAsync() helper methods that handled cluster mode batching. Added a test case to verify del() works correctly within a pipeline context. Reverted an unrelated pom.xml module addition to keep changes focused.

Refactor the system dialog implementation to accept Window objects instead of IWindowImpl for the parent parameter across all platform implementations. The current ISystemDialogImpl interface requires callers to extract PlatformImpl before passing the parent window, which creates an awkward API surface. Update src/Avalonia.Controls/Platform/ISystemDialogImpl.cs to change the parent parameter type from IWindowImpl to Window, then modify all implementations in src/Avalonia.Controls/SystemDialog.cs, src/Avalonia.DesignerSupport/Remote/Stubs.cs, src/Avalonia.Dialogs/ManagedFileDialogExtensions.cs, src/Avalonia.Native/SystemDialogs.cs, src/Avalonia.X11/NativeDialogs/GtkNativeFileDialogs.cs, and src/Windows/Avalonia.Win32/SystemDialogImpl.cs to work with Window objects directly and extract PlatformImpl internally where needed. Remove the IWindowImpl overload from Window.ShowDialog in src/Avalonia.Controls/Window.cs and update the corresponding tests in tests/Avalonia.Controls.UnitTests/WindowTests.cs to mock Window instead of IWindowImpl.

