The ISystemDialogImpl interface is forcing every caller to access PlatformImpl before showing a dialog, which is awkward and leaks implementation details. I should change ShowFileDialogAsync and ShowFolderDialogAsync to accept Window directly instead of IWindowImpl. This means updating the interface definition in ISystemDialogImpl.cs and then fixing all the platform-specific implementations. The Win32 SystemDialogImpl needs to access parent.PlatformImpl.Handle instead of parent.Handle, the GTK implementation needs to pass parent?.PlatformImpl to the internal ShowDialog method, and the macOS SystemDialogs class needs a helper method to extract the native window. The Window.ShowDialog method can be simplified by removing the IWindowImpl overload and just working with Window internally. Tests will need to mock Window instead of IWindowImpl for the parent parameter.

