Summary of the changes:

The system dialog API was refactored to accept Window objects directly instead of requiring IWindowImpl, simplifying the public interface and hiding platform implementation details. All platform-specific implementations were updated to extract PlatformImpl internally where needed, and the redundant IWindowImpl overload was removed from Window.ShowDialog. A safety fix was added to cache the platform implementation before async operations in the GTK dialog code to prevent potential race conditions.

Hey, I need to update our Go application build pipeline to give teams more flexibility with their base Docker images. Right now the edgeXBuildGoApp pipeline always uses Alpine-based images, but some projects need standard golang images without the Alpine suffix. This is causing issues for certain builds that depend on non-Alpine base images.

I want to add a new configuration option called useAlpineBase that lets teams choose whether they want Alpine-based images or standard golang images. When this flag is true (the default), we keep the current behavior with Alpine images. When it's false, we should use plain golang images without the -alpine suffix.

This change affects how we determine the base Docker image in the pipeline. I need to modify the getGoLangBaseImage function to accept this new parameter and return the appropriate image tag. The toEnvironment function also needs to read this config option and pass it along. Of course, I'll need to update the tests to cover both scenarios - when Alpine is enabled and when it's disabled.

Plan: 1. Update vars/edgeXBuildGoApp.groovy to add the alpineBased parameter to getGoLangBaseImage and modify the logic to return different images based on this flag. 2. Update the toEnvironment function to read useAlpineBase from config and pass it to getGoLangBaseImage. 3. Update test/edgeXBuildGoAppSpec.groovy to test both the true and false cases for the alpine flag, and add the useAlpineBase option to the config test cases.

