I need to ensure both the compression reader and resp.Body get closed properly. The compression reader should only be closed when we actually wrapped the body with one. I'll add an isWraped boolean flag that gets set to true in the gzip, deflate, and br cases. The deferred function will check this flag before closing the reader, and will always close resp.Body regardless. This prevents calling Close on the raw resp.Body twice while ensuring the compression reader's internal state gets cleaned up when needed.

