This PowerShell script is over 400 lines and contains all the logic for checking the current SDK version in global.json, downloading release notes from the dotnet/core repository, comparing versions, creating git branches, committing changes, and opening pull requests via the GitHub API. Functions like Get-Global-Json-Version, Get-Latest-SDK-Version, and Get-Latest-Runtime-Version handle the version detection, while the main script body manages the git operations and PR creation. Since the martincostello/update-dotnet-sdk action now provides all this functionality as a reusable workflow component, keeping this script in the repository is redundant. Removing it entirely simplifies the codebase and means we rely on the externally maintained action instead of our own implementation.

