# Add Text-to-Image Support for Discord Bot Conversations

The Discord bot currently proxies Coze service conversations but only handles text responses. When users request image generation through the bot, the response contains embedded images in Discord message embeds rather than plain text content. The current implementation does not capture or return these image URLs to the end user.

We need to extend the response handling to detect when a message contains embedded images and extract those image URLs. This requires modifying the response data structure to include an optional list of image URLs, updating the message listener to detect and process embeds in both message received and message update events, and ensuring the timeout is sufficient for image generation which typically takes longer than text responses.

Additionally, improving the logging output to include line numbers will help with debugging message handling issues.

Plan: 1. Update ChatResp.java to add embedImageUrls field for storing image URLs from message embeds. 2. Modify MessageListener.java to check for MessageEmbed objects in onMessageReceived and onMessageUpdate, extracting image URLs when present. 3. Increase the stream response timeout in MessageFuturesManager.java from 10 to 60 seconds to accommodate slower image generation. 4. Update logback.xml to include line numbers in console log output for better debugging.

