Recapping the work:

Extended the Discord bot conversation handling to support text-to-image responses by adding an embedImageUrls field to ChatResp for storing image URLs from message embeds. Updated MessageListener to detect and process MessageEmbed objects in both received and update events, extracting image URLs when present. Increased the stream response timeout from 10 to 60 seconds in MessageFuturesManager to accommodate slower image generation. Enhanced logging configuration to include line numbers for easier debugging.

Apply a monospaced font throughout the leaderboard interface to create a more technical, code-oriented aesthetic. The current design uses mixed fonts which creates visual inconsistency across contributor pages, activity feeds, and leaderboard cards. Additionally, address several minor spacing and alignment issues that affect readability on different screen sizes. Plan: 1. Update app/globals.css to set font-mono as the default body font. 2. Remove redundant font-mono classes from individual components since the global style now applies it. 3. Add font-inter back to specific text-heavy components like Markdown content for better readability. 4. Adjust font weights and colors in Header, GithubActivity, and other components for better visual hierarchy. 5. Clean up unused utility functions in lib/utils.ts. 6. Fix grid gap overflow issue in the leaderboard layout.

