Updated the remoteShell function to pass the debugPrint parameter through to the localShell call. This single-line change ensures that when debug printing is enabled, the constructed SSH command will be output before execution, matching the behavior of direct local shell commands.

Refactor the API client initialization logic to prevent redundant instance creation on every request. The current setup creates a new client object each time it is needed, which leads to excessive logging and potential performance overhead. Implement a singleton pattern to cache the client instance and only recreate it when configuration details change. Plan: 1. Create a singleton class to manage the client lifecycle. 2. Add configuration tracking to detect when a new instance is required. 3. Update the existing export function to delegate to the singleton manager.

