[uber/cadence: Cadence is a distributed, scalable, durable, and highly available orchestration engine to execute asynchronous long-running business logic in a scalable and resilient way.]

The shardscanner module implements workflow orchestration for scanning and repairing shard data across the distributed system. Currently, the workflow tests are scattered across a separate test helper package rather than residing alongside the implementation code they validate. This separation creates unnecessary indirection and negatively impacts code coverage metrics for the main shardscanner package.

The objective is to consolidate all workflow-related tests into the shardscanner package itself. This requires migrating the comprehensive workflow test suite from the auxiliary test package, removing the intermediate test helper workflows that previously wrapped the actual implementations, and ensuring all test registrations occur directly within the test setup. The existing unit tests for helper functions like batch index calculation and shard validation should remain in their current location but use distinct suite names to avoid conflicts with the incoming workflow tests.

This consolidation improves the accuracy of coverage reporting by ensuring tests are attributed to the package containing the actual implementation. It also simplifies the test architecture by eliminating an unnecessary abstraction layer between tests and the code they validate. The migration must preserve all existing test coverage including scanner workflow failure scenarios, fixer workflow success paths, corrupted keys retrieval logic, and all edge cases for configuration validation.

