This task addresses color format handling inconsistencies and adds support for a new color format in the LVGL graphics library. The RGB565A8 format was incorrectly reporting 24 bits per pixel when it should report 16 bits per pixel like RGB565, since the alpha channel is stored separately. A new ARGB8565 color format needs to be introduced with 24 bits per pixel (8-bit alpha followed by 16-bit RGB565), requiring updates to color format definitions, stride calculations, premultiplication logic, and binary decoder support. Additionally, the ffmpeg player integration requires proper stride calculation when initializing image descriptors. The affected files are src/misc/lv_color.c, src/misc/lv_color.h, src/draw/lv_draw_buf.c, src/libs/bin_decoder/lv_bin_decoder.c, and src/libs/ffmpeg/lv_ffmpeg.c.

