--- pkg/role/role.go ---
package role

const (
	System    = "system"
	Assistant = "assistant"
	User      = "user"
)

The existing code is locked to gpt-4o and doesn't account for the newer o1 family of models that OpenAI released. I need to start by adding the new model constants O1 and O1Mini to the models package, and while I'm there I should update DefaultModel to GPT4o since that's more current than GPT4. The role package also needs a Developer constant because o1 models expect a developer role instead of system for certain prompts. In the main example, I'll add a model flag so users can specify which model they want to use, defaulting to gpt-4o for backward compatibility. The CallAIandPrintResponse function needs to accept this model parameter and pass it through to the wrapper and key validation functions. I should extract the message building logic into its own GetMessages function since o1 models handle system prompts differently - they either use the developer role or combine the system prompt with the user prompt. The openai.go file needs updates too since isValidAIApiKey currently hardcodes gpt-4o in the validation URL and error messages. I'll make it accept the model parameter and use that dynamically instead.

